The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> has an all-new form factor with multiple folding and orientation options, and app developers are having some fun with it. You can find quite a few apps using the foldable display in unique ways, many with skeuomorphic designs.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/tiny-computer-iphone-duo.jpg" alt="" width="1179" height="663" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072619" /><br/>
<h2>Tiny Computers (&#36;3.99)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/tiny-computers/id6816896250">Tiny Computers</a> turns the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; into a miniature retro computer, with options inspired by the Macintosh, Commodore 64, Amiga 500, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/imac/">iMac</a> G3, iBook G3, and more. It works best with the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; in a seated orientation, giving you a display and a virtual keyboard.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Tiny Computers - for the iPhone Duo. Second look." src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/6jt_2bIaoxo" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
The mini computers have clickable keyboards, desktop games, and paint programs, along with hidden files and easter eggs.<br/>
<h2>Fold & Squish (Free)</h2><br/>
Made by the same developer as Tiny Computers, <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fold-squish-butterfly-paint/id6822789179">Fold &amp; Squish</a> lets you make Rorschach art with the Duo. You paint a design on one half of the Duo's display, close it, rub a finger over the outer display to "squish" the virtual paint, then open it up to see your finished design.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Fold &amp; Squish: Paint, Fold, Squish! Butterfly Art for iPhone, iPad &amp; Duo" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/OpPjzbRqBv0" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
An add-on "Sparkle Pack" includes glitter paints, rainbow paint, and pencil guides for helping you paint designs like butterflies, but the base feature set is available for free.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Portal (&#36;2.99/month)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/portal-escape-into-nature/id1436994560">Portal</a> is a relaxation app that offers "portals" to different natural environments, from a lava river in Iceland to the cloud forest in Costa Rica. There are over 100 locations, each with calming sounds and breathing exercises. The app can be used for meditation, but it also has focus timers and sleep timers.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/portal.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072620" /><br/>
When the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is unfolded, scenes take up the entire display, but it also works especially well when the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is in tent mode. There are three free portals to use that are refreshed each month, and a Premium subscription is priced at &#36;2.99 per month or &#36;29.99 per year.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Lake (Free)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/lake-coloring-book-for-adults/id1183717726">Lake</a> is an adult coloring book that's been updated for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. Holding the Duo in portrait mode gives you a full-page coloring surface, and the developer tells us it's being updated for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/lake-coloring-app.jpg" alt="" width="2048" height="1152" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072621" /><br/>
Lake has coloring pages from a long list of artists. It's free to download and comes with basic coloring pages and tools, but unlocking the full app requires a premium subscription that's &#36;9.99 per month.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Toastie (&#36;2.99)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/toastie-grilled-cheese-game/id6813841355">Toastie</a> turns the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; into a toaster for making grilled cheese sandwiches. It's a game where you prepare the sandwich ingredients, then close the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; to toast the sandwich. Timing is important, and the goal is to make a perfect grilled cheese.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">We turned the iPhone Duo into the world's most expensive toaster &#x1f96a;<br/>
<br/>
Build the sandwich quickly, then close your Duo to toast it. Don't burn it though!<br/>
<br/>
Check it out: https://t.co/riRVUFLlm1 https://t.co/0llh2lv9R1</p>&mdash; Tom Szykulski (@t_szykulski) <a href="https://x.com/t_szykulski/status/2107922328390672869?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">October 7, 2026</a></blockquote><br/>
<script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script></div><br/>
<h2>Delta Game Emulator (Free)</h2><br/>
Popular game emulator app Delta has been updated for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;, and it turns the Duo into a Nintendo DS.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p lang="ja" dir="ltr">iPhone DuoでDelta、折り畳むと笑う https://t.co/DySRV7UMBz</p>&mdash; たっくん＠超かぐプログラミング本 (@mikuta0407) <a href="https://x.com/mikuta0407/status/2113548402038563311?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">October 23, 2026</a></blockquote><br/>
<script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script></div><br/>
<br/>
The app has Nintendo DS controls, and when you close it, it looks like the shell of the gaming system and puts the game you're playing into sleep mode. Delta supports plenty of games from other systems too.<br/>
<h2>TypeDraw (&#36;4.99)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/typedraw/id6822194774">TypeDraw</a> turns the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; into a notebook. It looks like a notebook when the Duo is closed, and then you can open it up to pages you can write on. The app supports &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Taking notes on the iPhone Duo is so satisfying... especially when it looks and feels like a real notebook that truly belongs to you.<br/>
<br/>
With TypeDraw you choose what happens when you "open" your book, and you can personalise it with custom colours, fonts and even your own handwriting.<br/>
<br/>
For everyone lucky enough to have their hands on a Duo today: TypeDraw is available on the App Store now. For everyone else: it also looks and works great on regular iPhones &#x1f604;</p>&mdash; Phil Traut ᯅ (@SpatiallyMe) <a href="https://x.com/SpatiallyMe/status/2113598320861937741?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">October 23, 2026</a></blockquote><br/>
<script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script></div><br/>
<h2>Fold Accordion (&#36;2.99)</h2><br/>
As the name suggests, <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fold-accordion/id6815058989">Fold Accordion</a> turns the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; into an accordion. The hinge serves as the bellows, so the idea is to open and close the Duo to make music. There's a learn mode that lights up the keys you need to press.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/fold-accordion-app.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072622" /><br/>
<h2>Living Earth (&#36;5.99)</h2><br/>
If you're looking for an app that's ideal for the Duo's tent mode, <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/living-earth-clock-weather/id379869627">Living Earth</a> is worth checking out. It lets you set a location to get the time and local weather, plus it has a rotating globe that you can spin. When you unfold your &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;, the globe takes up the entire display.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/living-earth-iphone-duo.jpg" alt="" width="1440" height="701" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072623" /><br/>
The app shows live clouds, storms, and weather maps across the world, so you can keep track of hurricanes, tropical storms, and other weather events.<br/>
<h2>Duometry (&#36;2.99)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/duometry/id6814650592">Duometry</a> is a game that gives you a target angle you have to match by folding the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. The idea is to make your best guess at the angle, and then lock in to see if you were correct.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/duometry.jpg" alt="" width="2400" height="1600" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072624" /><br/>
<h2>Deck-Man (&#36;4.99)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/deck-man-cassette-player/id6817070335">Deck-Man</a> turns your &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; into a retro cassette player. You open up the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; to pick your music, insert the cassette, and then snap the Duo closed to start music playback.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/duo-man2.jpg" alt="" width="2048" height="1311" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067640" /><br/>
<h2>Orisuji (&#36;4.99)</h2><br/>
<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/orisuji/id6817092898">Orisuji</a> is a paper maze game where you start with the inner display, and then fold the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; to the outer display to solve the puzzles.<br/>
<br/>
